.TH KTX_CONVERT 1 "2026-10-27" "ktx (Rust port)" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ktx_convert \- convert a KTX1 texture to KTX2
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ktx
convert [OPTION...] <input\-file> <output\-file>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Converts a KTX version 1 file to KTX version 2, keeping the image data and translating the
metadata.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-input\-type <type>
Type of the input file (ktx).
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-map\-astc\-rgba\-to\-ldr
Map ASTC RGBA formats without an LDR/HDR hint to LDR.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-drop\-bad\-orientation
Drop invalid orientation metadata instead of failing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
ktx convert old.ktx new.ktx2
.fi
.SH NOTES
This is an unofficial Rust port of Khronos KTX\-Software (libktx and the ktx CLI); it is not
the Khronos build of the tool. The complete, current option list is printed by
.B ktx convert \-\-help.
.SH SEE ALSO
ktx(1)
